<title>CANADA: Canadian grain body estimates HRS wheat quality.</title>
<headline>Canadian grain body estimates HRS wheat quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission</p>
<p>on Monday released preliminary estimates of hard red spring</p>
<p>quality.</p>
<p>PROVINCE  Number of  Protein Content (PCT)</p>
<p>	    Samples    Mean Avg  Min. Max.</p>
<p>		 No1 Canada Western Red Spring</p>
<p>Man.	1,150	14.2	9.4  17.1</p>
<p>Sask.     4,605	12.9	9.1  17.7</p>
<p>Alta.     1,442	12.8	9.1  17.8</p>
<p>Prairies  7,197	13.1	9.1  17.8</p>
<p>		 No2 CWRS</p>
<p>Man.	1,384	14.3     10.3  17.9</p>
<p>Sask.     2,022	12.9	8.6  17.1</p>
<p>Alta.	 497	12.1	8.6  17.2</p>
<p>Prairies  3,903	13.3	8.6  17.9</p>
<p>		 No3 CWRS</p>
<p>Man.	  189	13.7     10.9  16.7</p>
<p>Sask.     1,331	12.1	8.5  17.2</p>
<p>Alta.	 975	11.8	8.0  16.1</p>
<p>Prairies  2,495	12.1	8.0  17.2</p>
<p>		 CW FEED</p>
<p>Man.	   54	14.2     11.0  16.3</p>
<p>Sask.	  35	12.7     10.2  14.5</p>
<p>Alta.	 109	12.1     10.1  14.8</p>
<p>Prairies    198	12.9     10.1  16.3</p>
<p>		 ALL GRADES</p>
<p>Man.	2,777	14.2	9.4  17.9</p>
<p>Sask.     7,993	12.8	8.5  17.7</p>
<p>Alta.     3,023	12.4	8.0  17.8</p>
<p>Prairies 13,793	13.0	8.0  17.9</p>
<p>N.B.: final quality estimates may be issued at the end of November or in early December, CGC spokesman Paul Graham said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
